<section id="install"><span class="compat-anchor" id="status" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Chart {{ release.chart.publishedVersion }} · application {{ release.chart.publishedAppVersion }}</h2>
<p>Requires Helm ≥3.8, Kubernetes ≥1.29 with native sidecars enabled, and a writable ReadWriteOnce StorageClass. Admission must allow a root init container with only <code>CHOWN</code> and <code>FOWNER</code>. The default <code>local-path</code> class is cluster-specific; select your own below.</p>
<p>This complete smoke installation starts only the broker with its built-in read-only CLI probe. It requires no chat/model/provider credentials and does not run an AI agent. Commands are for your selected cluster; inspect the render before installing.</p>
<pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Install the default broker and check its socket"><code># Set these two values for your cluster.
export KUBE_CONTEXT=your-context
export STORAGE_CLASS=your-rwo-class
helm template dekopon oci://ghcr.io/dekopon-agents/charts/dekopon \
  --version {{ release.chart.publishedVersion }} --namespace dekopon \
  --set-string state.storageClassName="$STORAGE_CLASS" \
  --set-string image.tag={{ release.tag }} --set-string image.digest={{ release.imageDigest }} &gt; rendered.yaml

helm upgrade --install dekopon \
  oci://ghcr.io/dekopon-agents/charts/dekopon \
  --version {{ release.chart.publishedVersion }} --kube-context "$KUBE_CONTEXT" \
  --namespace dekopon --create-namespace \
  --set-string state.storageClassName="$STORAGE_CLASS" \
  --set-string image.tag={{ release.tag }} --set-string image.digest={{ release.imageDigest }} --wait --timeout 10m
kubectl --context="$KUBE_CONTEXT" -n dekopon \
  rollout status deployment/dekopon --timeout=5m
kubectl --context="$KUBE_CONTEXT" -n dekopon exec deployment/dekopon \
  -c broker -- dekopon-brokerd probe --socket /run/dekopon/broker.sock</code>
</pre>
<p>The commands pin both the application tag and its multi-architecture image digest. A nonempty <code>image.digest</code> takes precedence over <code>image.tag</code>; with both empty, the chart uses its application version. Check the rendered image before installing.</p>
<p><strong>Expected:</strong> a ready broker container and probe exit 0, without output, after an authenticated capability-list exchange. The default config loads <code>cli-probe</code> but grants no executable capability; an empty authorized listing is healthy. The probe invokes nothing and emits no audit record. The site checks published chart metadata; it does not test a live cluster installation. Inspect the rendered resources before installing.</p>
</section>
<section id="upgrade">
<h2>Binaries, providers and saved state upgrade together.</h2>
<p>The application and chart have separate versions. Keep the gateway and broker binaries on one application release, check provider imports, and read the <a href="{{ source }}/docs/upgrading.md">pinned upgrade guide ↗</a> before replacing either.</p>
<ol>
<li>Save the current chart values, image digest, provider lock and configuration. Back up live rotating credentials and persistent state with the daemons stopped; an old login seed is not a usable credential backup.</li>
<li>Check the candidate broker configuration and gateway catalog against the candidate binaries. The optional <code>configCheck</code> hook runs those checks before rollout; its gateway <code>--probe</code> stage makes small paid requests to changed OpenRouter models. Supply candidate ConfigMaps and the referenced model-key environment variables explicitly.</li>
<li>Sync and precompile the selected managed providers, then roll the image and configuration together. Keep existing PVCs and their daemon-private subdirectories. Repeat the broker probe and a real chat/tool turn; restoring an older image alone does not restore compatible configuration or state.</li>
</ol>
<p>For installations predating the gateway rename, replace <code>dekopond</code> with <code>dekopon-gatewayd</code> and use <code>apiVersion: dekopon.dev/gatewayd/v1alpha1</code>. Update matching environment references, mount paths and the broker’s <code>dekopon-gatewayd</code> peer principal; there is no old-name executable alias.</p>
</section>
<section id="pod"><span class="compat-anchor" id="security" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="compat-anchor" id="one-pod" aria-hidden="true"></span>
<h2>Gateway-enabled pod and its mounts</h2>
<figure class="pod-map" aria-labelledby="pod-caption">
<div class="pod-inputs"><strong>Operator inputs</strong>
<p>Broker Secret / ConfigMap projections → <code>prepare-files</code> (root, CHOWN + FOWNER)</p>
<p>Copies broker inputs into broker-owned config tmpfs. Gateway config mounts separately as a read-only projection.</p>
</div>
<div class="pod-boundary">
<h3>One pod · one replica · Recreate deployment</h3>
<div class="pod-processes">
<div class="map-zone">
<h4>Gateway · UID 65533</h4>
<p><code>/etc/dekopon-gateway</code> ← read-only gateway-config projection</p>
<p>Catalog ← ConfigMap<br><code>/tmp</code> ← gateway disk scratch</p>
<p>Model/chat tokens ← gateway env or private rotating credential mount</p>
<p>↔ Outbound chat + model endpoints</p>
<p>Optional inbound webhook → Service → gateway listener</p>
</div>
<div class="map-zone broker-zone">
<h4>Broker · UID 65532</h4>
<p><code>/etc/dekopon</code> ← broker config + credentials only</p>
<p>Components ← image or managed provider store<br><code>/tmp</code> ← private tmpfs</p>
<p>Provider storage PVC + broker-only asset disk volume</p>
<p>Credential → native HTTP → permitted provider endpoint</p>
<p>No broker TCP listener</p>
</div>
</div>
<p class="pod-socket">Gateway ⇄ <code>/run/dekopon/broker.sock</code> ⇄ broker<br>Socket 0660 · directory 0710 · shared IPC GID 65534 · gateway pins server UID 65532</p>
<p class="pod-persistence">Retained state claim: distinct daemon-owned credential subdirectories, optional gateway journal/assets/wakes, and a managed-provider subdirectory mounted only in broker.</p>
</div>
<figcaption id="pod-caption">Both daemons → stdout / optional OTLP collector. Inbound routing and TLS are operator-owned; no Service or Ingress is created by default. The gateway is off in the smoke installation above.</figcaption>
</figure>
<p>The same kernel and shared socket are required for peer authentication and descriptor passing. Do not split this into remote broker/gateway Deployments or scale replicas against the same state. Daemons have read-only roots, no added capabilities and RuntimeDefault seccomp; this is not a production-hardening claim.</p>
<p><code>console.enabled: true</code> (chart {{ release.chart.publishedVersion }}) adds one more idle container to the same pod: UID 65535, IPC group only, no credentials, for <code>kubectl exec -it … -c console -- dekopon-console</code>. It needs <code>gateway.enabled</code> and its own broker attestor grant for <code>console.subject</code>. Its default image inherits the daemon image, which already contains the console; <code>console.image</code> can override that pin.</p>
